-- 0112 - v1.100.0: the hotel list the CEO supplied, as data.
--
-- 442 hotels and 690 named contacts, read from 1. DATA HOTEL.xlsx on
-- 05-09-2026 - one worksheet per state, which is where the state list in
-- 0111 comes from. Ids are written explicitly and every insert is OR IGNORE,
-- so applying this file twice changes nothing.
--
-- WHAT WAS CLEANED ON THE WAY IN, once, here, rather than in every query
-- that reads it later:
--   - Columns were found by HEADER, not by letter. Selangor carries a
--     CONTACT 4 column, which pushes capacity and star rating one place
--     right on that sheet alone.
--   - A contact cell in the workbook is a block of text - name, then one or
--     two numbers, then an email. It is split into its parts here.
--   - Phone numbers are written in Malaysian form: 01X-XXX XXXX for a
--     mobile, 0X-XXXX XXXX for a landline, with ext kept where it was given.
--     Cells holding two numbers with no separator were split.
--   - Text is plain ASCII, because a migration the remote D1 parser has to
--     read is not the place for a curly quote.

